    "body": "## Independent exact-head review - Chat03B2 synthetic SQLite schema feasibility\n\n**HEAD reviewed:** `f11dd978ca12f19b5c1f0463bf9d239521aa4eba`. Parent is the exact PR441 HEAD `6ad90e6e86d528b1858776477fb7e8680f89115d`; PR442 stays OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, mergeable clean. Compare is ahead 1, behind 0; **only two test files** added: `gameplay-server/test/fixtures/chat03b2_schema_v4_probe.sql` (254 lines) and `gameplay-server/test/test_chat03b2_schema_v4_probe.py` (479 lines). No runtime migration/Worker changes.\n\n**Narrow PASS:** The executable SQLite-only experiment rebuilds the existing creation table and exercises rollback, state and FK constraints, live-row recovery material closure, digest-preserving tombstones and synthetic cross-connection races. Exact-head GitHub Actions checked independently: [CAS 39958135952](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39958135952) SUCCESS with job log showing all 17 newly discovered tests and **39/39 Python tests**; [Private API 39958135917](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39958135917) SUCCESS; [Forensics 39958136534](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39958136534) SUCCESS. Existing workerd checks were rerun, but the proposed new v4 probe was NOT run through D1. Local test/policy claims from Codex are not independently reproduced here.\n\n**Two blocking overclaims for a safe eventual migration:**\n1. The fixture builds `chat03b2_recovery_eligibility` from **current** `gameplay_battle_capabilities.token_sha256` plus a synthetic `expected_generation=<redacted>\n2. `request_fingerprint_sha256 TEXT NOT NULL` is preserved for `TOMBSTONE`, and `_close(..., 'TOMBSTONE')` does not clear it. This is not the previously required minimal **idempotency-digest-only** tombstone: the request fingerprint derives from the participants and survives battle deletion. Make it nullable in tombstone state, clear it atomically on transition, and add assertions that the retired row retains no battle, fingerprint, deadline or recovery materials.\n\n**Scope boundary:** `_commit` and `_scheduler_terminal` are Python transaction simulations, not the actual `gameplay_apply_transition` SQL auth fence or a D1 protected scheduler view. Concurrency proves selected SQLite `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` serial orders, not hosted D1 authorization or both guaranteed outcomes. This does not invalidate the narrow experiment, but it must not be presented as generation-aware Worker security or deployable v4 migration.\n\n**Disposition:** `PASS_NARROW_SYNTHETIC_SQLITE_MECHANICS / BLOCKED_MIGRATION_ELIGIBILITY_AND_TOMBSTONE_PRIVACY`. Keep PR442 Draft; request a narrow two-file correction in its existing Codex implementation thread, preserve previous tests and checkpoint. Do not merge or deploy. Cloudflare, hosted D1, real-human trust-model and retention approvals remain out of scope.",
